rd  dream in front of a picture of donald  trump  is that um or does that in any way sum  up for you the the trump era  um no not really i i was here for the  last nine months or so  of the trump administration but i also  saw it from from new york which was my  previous posting  i mean it's the job of the british  ambassador it's the job of the british  prime minister  to get on with the american president of  the day  and defend british interests and british  values  and that's what we do regardless of  who's in the white house  we're very much looking forward to  working with president biden and  vice president harris there is so much  to do to get covid recovery  underway and get economies back on track  and we really look forward to being able  to cooperate with them on climate  as well as all the bedrock security  relationship that we have  yes i'm going to persist with looking  backwards before i look forwards if you  don't mind  um unpredictable attention seeking we  know  how hard was it for you to get on with  donald trump and his administration  well there were areas where we disagreed  on policy  uh iran would be one climate tariffs  and where we disagree on policy we say  so we speak out  we defend british interests but it is  the job of the british ambassador here  to get on with the american  administration of the day  because fundamentally regardless of  who's in the white house or  who's in government in the uk the  bedrock of the relationship it's a very  deep profound  successful relationship built on  security and defense  built on a common culture and that  always carries us through  so what does your job involve now you as  ambassador is it time to  to get the elbows out get the attention  of the new guys does your competitive  street come out do you think to  to get noticed amongst all those other  ambassadors who are vying for attention  uh it is a bit of a competition i think  that's a fair comment  but at the same time we all want to  cooperate we all want to support  the biden harris administration as they  get their agenda  underway for britain particularly i'll  be concentrating on supporting the prime  minister  and the foreign secretary on all the g7  work  that's where we'll be doing the bulk of  international cooperation  on covid recovery and that also involves  you know looking at technology  bringing democracies and technologically  advanced countries together  it's great to be able to do that with  america and then we'll be putting a lot  of emphasis in the embassy  on climate uh britain hosts cop 26 with  italy  in glasgow in november and now that we  have a biden administration ready to  come back into  the climate agreement the paris  agreement there's a lot we can do  together  and then i think the other priority for  us immediately  is to get a group of vaccines to make  sure that the world health organization  is working well to help us learn lessons  from this pandemic help us avoid future  ones and get vaccines around the world  to developing countries and others well  we've got a picture of uh boris johnson  watching all of this  unfold on television back in london  let's listen also to what he had to say  really congratulate uh joe and kamala  harris on uh on their achievement on  their inauguration  uh today it's a fantastic uh thing for  america it's a  step forward uh for the for the country  it's been through  a bumpy period and for us and america  it's a big moment we've got uh things we  want to do  together uh you mentioned obviously  there's two big  international events which the uk is  hosting uh on climate change and the g7  which will no doubt  help relations also vaccines you didn't  mention  a trade deal there was almost a sense  wasn't there that donald trump was going  to be the great facilitator of that  is it still viable is it on the table  does it  go in the back seat do you think because  joe biden is in office and he wasn't  such a fan of  of brexit where do 